{:edb/db-before-t 1437 :edb/db-after-t 1438 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534750 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:49:44.100Z" 13194139534750 true] [17592186105525 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139534750 false] [17592186105525 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139534750 true] [17592186105525 1145 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-4)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1; 0x + 0y = 0\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation\n\n$$\n0x+0y = 0\n$$\n\nwe can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y)$, we get\n\n$$\nx=1+3y\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\nx = 1 + 3y; y = y\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 + 3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = ⟨1 + 3y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)\n$$" 13194139534750 false] [17592186105525 1145 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y=1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534750 true] [17592186105526 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=4 \\\\ 4x+10y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 true] [17592186105526 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n$2x + 5y = 4; 4x + 10y = 0$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 false] [17592186105526 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{5}{2}y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534750 true] [17592186105526 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & R_{1}\\end{vmatrix}:=\\frac{1}{2}R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + (-4)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\nx + \\frac{5}{2}y = 2; 0x + 0y =-8\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation\n\n$$\n0x+0y=-8\n$$\n\nhas no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8$, which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534750 false] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307559 13194139534750 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307573 13194139534750 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307593 13194139534750 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307600 13194139534750 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307613 13194139534750 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307552 13194139534750 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307566 13194139534750 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307580 13194139534750 true] [17592186106243 1017 #edb/ref 17592186103967 13194139534750 false] [17592186106243 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307587 13194139534750 true] [17592186106243 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534750 true] [17592186106243 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-6y=2 \\\\ -4x+24y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 true] [17592186106243 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${x - 6y = 2; - 4x + 24y =-10$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 false] [17592186106243 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 24 & -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 24 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-6y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-2$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-2,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534750 true] [17592186106245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186103979 13194139534750 false] [17592186106245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307607 13194139534750 true] [17592186106245 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534750 true] [17592186106245 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7x+14y=21 \\\\ 3x+6y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 true] [17592186106245 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${7x + 14y = 21; 3x + 6y = 9$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 false] [17592186106245 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307552 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307553 13194139534750 true] [17592186307552 1089 "q-130923" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307552 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534750 true] [17592186307552 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ -4x+8y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534750 true] [17592186307552 1113 #uuid "d891d6e7-8e53-5283-b451-783d6b61c60e" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307552 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307554 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307555 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307556 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307557 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307558 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1041 "selection" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307555 13194139534750 true] [17592186307553 1110 #uuid "6ae3b192-27d3-5a52-b4a6-108fa9bcc17c" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307554 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534750 true] [17592186307554 1111 #uuid "f08aee29-d635-5a36-8dc2-2e6082fcdb62" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307555 1034 "No solution" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534750 true] [17592186307555 1111 #uuid "f4a99e56-614c-5c40-a70a-dc986e138a3b" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307556 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534750 true] [17592186307556 1111 #uuid "1dfd9d13-3564-53de-a254-ff7c3a73fbda" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307557 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534750 true] [17592186307557 1111 #uuid "0876b98f-b15c-56f4-ab14-4427e5b26dcd" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307558 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534750 true] [17592186307558 1111 #uuid "eb49d7ca-5515-5bc3-8ed9-29b0b18758de" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307559 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307560 13194139534750 true] [17592186307559 1089 "q-20782" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307559 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534750 true] [17592186307559 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139534750 true] [17592186307559 1113 #uuid "8ab34347-482c-500f-9bf4-3eb466e5cadc" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307559 1145 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=-3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307561 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307562 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307563 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307564 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307565 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1041 "selection" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307561 13194139534750 true] [17592186307560 1110 #uuid "6bb0dbaf-c46c-5ba7-8849-0019323bebec" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307561 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534750 true] [17592186307561 1111 #uuid "a2c8b603-da2c-547e-b192-9b2d550f9286" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307562 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534750 true] [17592186307562 1111 #uuid "0ef3fb7a-5973-50ad-b9f7-22b8f6264b8c" 13194139534750 true] [17592186307563 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\beg